# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SentinelOps .gitignore
# Tells git which files to NOT track. Grouped by reason.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Secrets & local config (NEVER commit these) --------------
# .env files hold passwords, DB credentials, API keys. Keeping
# them out of git is a primary defense against secret leakage.
.env
.env.*
# ...but DO allow a committed template that lists the *names* of
# required variables with no real values:
!.env.example

# --- Dependencies (reproducible from lockfiles) ---------------
node_modules/

# --- Build / compiled output ----------------------------------
# Go compiles to binaries; the frontend builds to /dist.
/backend/bin/
/backend/tmp/
*.exe
*.exe~
dist/
/frontend/dist/

# --- Go test / profiling artifacts ----------------------------
*.test
*.out

# --- Logs -----------------------------------------------------
*.log

# --- Editor & OS noise ----------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
